WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.050
Ever gotten a message that just says,

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.450
can we talk tomorrow?

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.300
And suddenly your brain starts preparing for a disaster

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.240
that hasn't even happened yet?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.650
Here's the thing.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:13.350
Anxiety is your brain's alarm system.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.340
Its whole job is to protect you.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.490
Sometimes it just treats an ordinary moment like a five

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:19.920
alarm emergency.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.190
Your brain isn't your enemy.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.270
It's just being a little too protective.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.130
So what does that look like?

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.570
Replaying a conversation from three years ago.

00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:32.530
A racing heart and sweaty hands.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.390
Avoiding that one email.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:38.000
Or a tiny problem growing into a giant monster in your

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.290
imagination.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.910
Which one sounds most familiar?

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.030
Take a second.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:43.850
Really.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.370
And when it shows up,

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:46.490
you've got options.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.530
First, name it.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.270
I'm feeling anxious right now.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.480
A feeling is not automatically a fact.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.140
Next, ground yourself.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.530
Name five things you can see.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:57.660
Four you can touch.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.990
Three you can hear.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.450
It pulls you right back into the present.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:02.540
And finally,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:03.590
slow down.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.070
One gentle breath.

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:09.010
You don't have to solve every problem in your head today.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:09.720
Remember,

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.920
your brain is trying to protect you.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.350
You just don't have to believe every scary story it tells

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:15.950
you.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.350
And if anxiety starts running your everyday life,

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.760
talking to a professional is a strong move,

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:22.750
not a weakness.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:23.570
Now tell me,

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.130
what's your brain's favorite way of overthinking?

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.180
Drop your answer in the comments.
